                        "form": "феру́лах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af9f82e8-e0f8-3332-a58c-a84d9d7ea90f",
                        "entry_id": "422cad54-f645-318a-b2e4-98d9443965cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. истор. линейка для наказания, которой били по ладони провинившегося ученика в школе"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ee0175b-213a-44df-b710-d2814458eb8c",
                                "sense_id": "af9f82e8-e0f8-3332-a58c-a84d9d7ea90f",
                                "text": "В большей части школ, впрочем, господствует еще прежняя учительская ферула, и телесные наказания находят до сих пор многих защитников в американских школах."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4c2384ff-f584-30d6-a777-35113f503800",
                        "entry_id": "422cad54-f645-318a-b2e4-98d9443965cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн., устар. гнетущий и бдительный надзор, гнетущая стеснительная опека, строгое обращение"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "73a70579-43bd-4f6a-aa37-3e0125d56f50",
                                "sense_id": "4c2384ff-f584-30d6-a777-35113f503800",
                                "text": "Выпустили вы его из-под вашей ферулы, смотрите, - а он опять отплясывает комаринскую."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74d4060f-5e2a-45b8-b4df-0e1e58d23dd8",
                                "sense_id": "4c2384ff-f584-30d6-a777-35113f503800",
                                "text": "Тогда у Полины была ещё жива мать, <…> девушке, весьма естественно, хотелось освободиться из-под этой ферулы и вырваться из скучной провинциальной жизни."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59043e8e-00cb-49cc-92b0-a99793572d37",
                        "source_entry_id": "422cad54-f645-318a-b2e4-98d9443965cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "ferule",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ferule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                        "entry_id": "3907ddc5-41ed-3e43-bd95-70efcb4fa7ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ruler-shaped instrument, generally used to slap naughty children on the hand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fab238f6-9cc5-4241-bf45-0ac239a0203c",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                                "text": "In his hand he swayed a ferule, that sceptre of despotic power; the birch of justice reposed on three nails behind the throne, a constant terror to evil doers, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31c7365a-5143-4f8e-b9da-a8b6613dd2bf",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                                "text": "He [a midshipman] lords it over those below him, while lorded over himself by his superiors. It is as if with one hand a school-boy snapped his fingers at a dog, and at the same time received upon the other the discipline of the usher's ferule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5eeddfa0-067b-4c8a-8c0f-b9c00e3eb5b5",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                                "text": "The master, who stood at the end of the room, with a huge ferule under his arm, bent full upon me a look of stern appeal; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9538bcfe-0d72-4570-8844-8e983775200a",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                                "text": "The schoolmaster, always severe, grew severer and more exacting than ever, for he wanted the school to make a good showing on \"Examination\" day. His rod and his ferule were seldom idle now—at least among the smaller pupils."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a66192c5-09ce-4059-8d5e-8cf8649e6954",
                                                "sense_id": "e1a70be9-36ff-3eed-81d6-8e562b711d39",
                                                "text": "It is to keep a man awake, to keep him alive to his own soul and its fixed design of righteousness, that the better part of moral and religious education is directed; not only that of words and doctors, but the sharp ferule of calamity under which we are all God’s scholars till we die."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ferule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8928feb9-8bcc-3b8c-be7b-76417e8fe711",
                                        "entry_id": "2175e6d3-f46c-346d-8a65-a2c0580d391c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To punish with a ferule."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebdb39fc-6514-420e-b142-06e4972d5a74",
                                                "sense_id": "8928feb9-8bcc-3b8c-be7b-76417e8fe711",
                                                "text": "And they were right in their assumption; I could cudgel a great lubberly delinquent of a boy[…]but when it came to feruling a girl[…]my manhood rebelled[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
